# Layouts & module routes

Full spec: **[docs/layouts.md](../docs/layouts.md)**. Combine with [rendering.md](../docs/rendering.md), [app-states.md](../docs/app-states.md).

## Route ownership

- Each **URL prefix** belongs to **one** `module/<feature>/`; all child pages use that module’s Tier 2 layout and pages.
- Do **not** add layout or nav logic in `apps/*/src/app` — **import only** from `module/`.

## Two tiers (required)

| Tier | Path | Contains |
|------|------|----------|
| **1 Shell** | `module/studio-shell/client/studio/` | Sidebar + inset + **primary header**; nav varies by module via **config**, not duplicate layouts |
| **2 Section** | `module/<feature>/client/studio/layout/` | **Sub-header** (title, optional tabs, section actions); **shared by all child routes** in that section |
| **Page** | `module/<feature>/server/page` + `client/…/rsc` | Content column only — no duplicate sub-header on leaf pages |

If two pages share the same sub-header/tabs → **one** `client.section.layout.tsx`.

## Naming

- `client.shell.*` — Tier 1  
- `client.section.*` — Tier 2  
- `client.page.*` — page body (content slot)

## Legacy

- Do **not** extend `apps/studio/src/components/layout` or fat `app/**/layout.tsx` for new work — rewrite into `module/studio-shell` + module `layout/`.

## States & shift

- Put `loading.tsx` on the **fetching segment**; skeleton matches **Tier 2 sub-header + content** height ([app-states.md](../docs/app-states.md)).
- Tier 1 stable when switching Tier 2 children; Tier 2 stable when switching leaf pages.

## Forbidden

- Module-specific tabs in Tier 1 shell (except global nav).
- Per-page sub-headers when siblings should share Tier 2.
- Cross-module layout imports (use `@loftlancer/ui` + route helpers).
